"Don't eat leperchauns! They

give you a twitchy feeling or something, and you teleport around for
the rest of the game! "


I respectfully (as a mere novice) disagree: eating leprechauns gives you 
free teleportation with no power cost, and this can be very useful once 
you have either levitation or teleport control via rings. With 
levitation you will avoid trap damage I think if you drop on to one, and 
with teleport control (the preferred option) you can move or not if you 
choose. So it's a kind of free rail ticket once you have a safe way. 
Most useful when moving in already explored levels because it speeds 
progres up immensly.

Best is combined levitation and teleport control.

By the way, as a dog-lover, I think I ought to be able to pick up and 
carry my little dog if i feel like it. Then I could get hime over lava, 
water etc with out a magic whistle. Also, I don't see why Ii should not 
be able to apply a collar as well as a leash-an amulet might be useful 
for example. One sometimes has a spare. And could there not be a nethack 
(or in my case Falcon's Eye) equivalent of the cold-weather canine 
jacket ? I am thinking of the waxed jacket type for maximum 
protection-might last longer than grease.

And on the subject of pets, ie tame monsters, one should surely be able 
to remove items and replace them with better ones when the pet can wear 
armour and wield weapons ? I'd like to provide my tame Elf Lord with 
Excalibur and Crystal Plate Mail surplus to my own requirements.

